// SWARM RABBIT HOLE — Wave 15 (Impl-T, Cohort Delta): Salt ε — the
// E0701 all-or-nothing rejection, PRODUCT arm (A4 §4's rule 1). A
// variable×variable product in a VERIFIED function's contract is Tier
// N — never dischargeable (MRDP; the §1(v) nonlinear cliff) — and the
// verified tier is all-or-nothing by design: no silent degradation
// inside a verified fn. The diagnostic names the offending atom, the
// rule, and the bounded-degree redemption clause (degrade is a total
// function of (atom shape × known bounds), not a blanket rule).

verified fn area(int w, int h) -> int requires(w * h > 0) {
    return w * h
}

fn main() {
    print(area(3, 4))
}
